1
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:47,739
WARNING: May Cause Toe-Tapping.

2
00:09:23,478 --> 00:09:29,478
Happy Feet is a animation, comedy, family film directed by George Miller.

3
00:14:05,217 --> 00:14:11,217
Into the world of the Emperor Penguins, who find their soul mates
through song, a penguin is born who cannot sing.

4
00:18:46,956 --> 00:18:52,956
But he can tap dance something fierce!

5
00:23:28,695 --> 00:23:34,695
Mumble (voice), played by Elijah Wood.

6
00:28:10,434 --> 00:28:16,434
Ramon / Lovelace (voice), played by Robin Williams.

7
00:32:52,173 --> 00:32:58,173
Gloria (voice), played by Brittany Murphy.

8
00:37:33,913 --> 00:37:39,913
Memphis (voice), played by Hugh Jackman.

9
00:42:15,652 --> 00:42:21,652
Norma Jean (voice), played by Nicole Kidman.

10
00:46:57,391 --> 00:47:03,391
Noah (voice), played by Hugo Weaving.

11
00:51:39,130 --> 00:51:45,130
Happy Feet is a 2006 animated jukebox musical comedy film directed and produced by George
Miller and written by Miller, John Collee, Judy Morris and Warren Coleman.

12
00:56:20,869 --> 00:56:26,869
It stars Elijah Wood, Robin Williams, Brittany Murphy, Hugh Jackman, Nicole Kidman,
Hugo Weaving, Anthony LaPaglia, Magda Szubanski and Steve Irwin.

13
01:01:02,608 --> 01:01:08,608
In the film, Mumble, a tap-dancing emperor penguin who lacks the ability to sing a heartsong to attract a soulmate and is ridiculed by his
peers and family, departs on a journey across Antarctica to learn what is causing the local fish population to decline.

14
01:05:44,347 --> 01:05:50,347
Happy Feet was the first animated film produced by
Kennedy Miller and Animal Logic.

15
01:10:26,086 --> 01:10:32,086
An international co-production between the United States and Australia, the film was
produced at Sydney-based visual effects and animation studio Animal Logic.

16
01:15:07,826 --> 01:15:13,826
The film was released in North America on 17 November
2006 and in Australia on 26 December.

17
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
A planned IMAX 3D release was cancelled due to budgetary issues.

18
01:24:31,304 --> 01:24:37,304
Happy Feet received generally positive reviews from critics, with praise for its visuals, storyline and songs, and
grossed $384 million against its $100 million budget, becoming the tenth-highest-grossing film of 2006.

19
01:29:13,043 --> 01:29:19,043
It earned the inaugural BAFTA Award for Best Animated Film, and the Academy Award for Best Animated
Feature, and was nominated for the Annie Award and the Saturn Award for Best Animated Feature.

20
01:33:54,782 --> 01:34:00,782
A sequel, Happy Feet Two, was released in 2011.

21
01:38:36,521 --> 01:38:42,521
The film explores themes of fish, ocean, zoo, penguin, tap dancing.

22
01:43:18,260 --> 01:43:24,260
The tone is lighthearted.
